c 15:11 4Mac 15:18 * ;] \nto turn about, turn (Hom., al., but not found in Att..) : with accusative, Jas.4:9 (WH, txt.; cf. μεταστρέφω).†\n (AS)","source_line":3457}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"converterá","count":1},{"gloss":"perverter","count":1}]},"G3542":{"id":"G3542","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3542","disambiguated_id":"G3542 =","unique_id":"G3542","headword":"νομή","transliteration":"nomē","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"pasture","definition_en":"νομή, -ῆς, ἡ\n (νέμω, to pasture), [in LXX chiefly for מִרְעֶה, also for נָוֶה, etc. ;] \n__1. a pasture, pasturage: figuratively, Jhn.10:9 \n __2. a grazing, feeding; metaphorically, of a spreading sore, 2Ti.2:17 (Polyb.).†\n (AS)","source_line":3655}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"pasto","count":1},{"gloss":"gangrena","count":1}]},"G3699":{"id":"G3699","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3699","disambiguated_id":"G3699 =","unique_id":"G3699","headword":"ὅπου","transliteration":"hopou","lexical_morphology":"G:CONJ","gloss_en":"where(-ever)","definition_en":"ὅπου \n adv. \nof place, correlat. of ποῦ (which see), where. \n __I. Prop., of place, \n __1. where; \n __(a) in relative sentences, with indic: Mat.25:24, 26, Mrk.2:4 4:5, 15 5:40 13:14, Jhn.3:8 6:62 7:34, 36 11:32 14:3 17:24 20:19, Rom.15:20, Rev.2:13; after nouns of place, for relat. prepositional phrase (ἐν ᾧ., etc.), Mat.6:19-20 13:5 26:57 28:6, Mrk.6:55 9:48 Luk.12:33, Jhn.1:28 4:20, 46 6:23 7:42 10:40 11:30 12:1 18:1, 20 19:18, 20 19:41 20:12, Act.17:1, Rev.2:13 11:8 20:10; before ἐκεῖ., Mat.6:21, Luk.12:34 17:37 Jhn.12:26; id. pleonast. (= Heb. שָׁם . . . אֲשֶׁר; Aram. תַּמָּן . . דּ; of. Gen.13:3), ὅ. . . . ἐκεῖ, Rev.12:6, 14; ὅ. . . . ἐπ᾽ αὐτῶν, Rev.17:9; ὅ. ἄν, wherever (M, Pr., 168), with imperfect indic., Mrk.6:56; with Pres. subjc., Mat.24:28; ὅ. ἐάν, Mat.26:13, Mrk.6:10 9:18 14:9, 14 a; \n __(b) in quaest. indir., with aor. subjc.: Mrk.14:14 b, Luk.22:11. \n __2. In late writers (sometimes also in cl.; Bl., § 25, 2), with verbs of motion, = ὅποι, whither: with indic., Jhn.8:21-22 13:33, 36 14:4 21:18, Heb.6:20, Jas.3:4; ὅ. ἄν, whithersoever, with present ind., Rev.14:4; subjc., Luk.9:57; ὅ. ἐάν, Mat.8:19. \n __II. Without strict local sense, \n __1. of time or condition: Col.3:11, Heb.9:16 10:18, Jas.3:16, 2Pe.2:11. \n __2. Of cause or reason (AV, whereas): 1Co.3:3.†\n (AS)","source_line":3815}],"occurrence_count":81,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"onde","count":76},{"gloss":"aonde","count":5}]},"G3712":{"id":"G3712","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3712","disambiguated_id":"G3712 =","unique_id":"G3712","headword":"ὀργυιά","transliteration":"orguia","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"a fathom","definition_en":"ὀργυιά, -ᾶς, ἡ\n (ὀρέγω), \nthe length of the outstretched arms, a fathom: Act.27:28.†\n (AS)","source_line":3829}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"braças","count":2}]},"G4141":{"id":"G4141","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4141","disambiguated_id":"G4141 =","unique_id":"G4141","headword":"πλήσσω","transliteration":"plēssō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to strike","definition_en":"πλήσσω \n [in LXX chiefly for נָכָה hi., ho. ;] \nto strike, smite: pass., Rev.8:12 (cf. ἐπι, πλήσσω).†\n (AS)","source_line":4266}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"ferida","count":1}]},"G4449":{"id":"G4449","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4449","disambiguated_id":"G4449 =","unique_id":"G4449","headword":"πυρράζω","transliteration":"purrazō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"be (fiery) red","definition_en":"πυρράζω\n (πυρρός), [in LXX, πυρρίζω: Lev.13:19, 42 ff. Lev.14:37 (אֲדַמְדָּם) * ;] \nto be fiery red: Mat.16:2-3.†\n (AS)","source_line":4582}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"bom","count":1},{"gloss":"tempestade","count":1}]},"G4577":{"id":"G4577","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"s